{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a set of five numbers, the average of two of the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the average of the other three numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The average of all five numbers is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a318476e8ad766c6f60c1c7f8509faa33dd1d4ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 8 \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 8 \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 8 \\frac{3}{4} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 9 \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"385\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the average of all numbers, we can first find the sum of all of the numbers using the averages of the two groups, and then divide them by the number of numbers (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in this case).\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae90d71491f591ab5a16d19ee7629e8226ec9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> represent the sum of the numbers of the first group of numbers (the one with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> elements), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6c5ddfd368673c178f3323ce2994cdbc8fbdab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> represent the sum of the numbers in the other group. Setting up equations, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/4441eef14c5daa3e85f77043e983cdb18aefd06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s_1}{2} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b19d2cbb8f10e316624ea14f74e7074a01d4eab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1 = 2 \\times 12 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/695d4968f32c24ae0bc3268db01ce7e238c411b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s_2}{3} = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56911f0d3880756724ea6515e647502d5bc7728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_2 = 3 \\times 7 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>The sum of all of the number is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8ab950bc56f9209cb32e7b16c9e96838200452b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1 + s_2 = 24 + 21 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The average of all the numbers can then be found with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4a31d862b2c10a327c32e0f63ca65f6420202a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45}{5} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192800\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 50/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2492/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:34004:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192800 and revision id 260690. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}